  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01. I handled 12 items: the 8 that were there at the start and 4 that arrived while I worked. 11 are closed. 1 is left open on purpose. A few items need you.\n\n**Needs you:**\n- **Brennan (pt-0008): critical potassium.** The lab now says the sample was not hemolyzed, so the 6.4 is considered real. A stat BMP is ordered for today. On-call has the stat alert, and he has a corrected message to come in today.\n- **Misfiled fax (Nowicki, pt-0065):** a Lakeshore addendum (8 mm nodule, Lung-RADS 4A, LDCT in 3 months) was filed to her chart. Only the name matches; the DOB and MRN are another patient's, and no Riverbend patient has them. I took no clinical action in her chart and asked Dr. Iyer urgently to send it to the right patient's clinician. The document needs to be moved out of her chart.\n- **Orders I couldn't withdraw (no tool):**\n  - Brennan: the urgent repeat BMP (sr-t0011) is replaced by today's stat BMP.\n  - Patel: the 12-month LDCT (sr-t0015) and its tracking task (task-t0016) are replaced by the 6-month LDCT.\n  - Please discontinue them.\n\n**Each patient:**\n- **Patel (pt-0006)**\n  - CT urogram 10-19: nothing explains the hematuria. Further workup (e.g., urology/cystoscopy) is your call; I didn't order it. The 4 mm left lower lobe nodule is the one already followed in lung screening.\n  - I first ordered the next screening LDCT on the 12-month schedule. Then a Lakeshore addendum arrived: the 04-14 LDCT now shows a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule, Lung-RADS 3, with LDCT in 6 months.\n  - The window runs 09-14 to 11-14 and is still open. I ordered the LDCT by 11-14 with a tracking task due 11-14, sent him a corrected message, and wrote notes.\n  - His chart conflicts: your H&P says current smoker, about 42 pack-years; the smoking-status entry says ex-smoker.\n- **Ondricka (pt-0016):**\n  - TSH is normal.\n  - The potassium of 6.3 was corrected to 4.4 (analyzer fault).\n  - Both closed with no action.\n- **Parisian (pt-0007)**\n  - CT angiogram: the preliminary read was superseded by the final. There is no PE and no nodule, and no lung follow-up is needed. Closed.\n  - BMP 10-22: creatinine 1.64, up from 0.98 about 35 hours earlier, which meets the kidney-injury rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by Mon 10-26, messaged him, and wrote a note.\n  - He has ibuprofen from the ED, naproxen as needed, and had IV contrast on 10-20. I flagged these for your review and made no medication change.\n  - **Left open:** a chest X-ray from 10-22 that arrived this morning. It is preliminary only (possible 7 mm right upper lobe nodule) and no final report exists yet, so the policy says to leave it open.\n- **Whitfield (pt-0033)**\n  - Creatinine 1.31 on 10-22: I excluded the entered-in-error 0.84. Against the 1.27 from 10-17 it does not meet the kidney-injury rule. Closed with no action.\n  - A later urgent-care creatinine arrived: 1.78 the same evening, up 0.47 in about 9 hours, which meets the rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10-26, messaged her, and wrote a note.\n- **Brennan (pt-0008)**\n  - The potassium of 6.4 was first flagged hemolyzed. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP and messaged him to come in by Monday.\n  - The lab then corrected it: the hemolysis comment belonged to another patient's sample. I switched to the not-hemolyzed rule as above and wrote a note.\n  - His medication list has no potassium-raising drug, so nothing was held. I left metoprolol in place for safety.\n\nThe messages queue has 6 refill requests from before I started. They were outside this task and I left them untouched.",
